{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8EcShSQhFDywHXBTHd5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Firecrawl looks cheaper at this volume, but only by a small margin.** The Tavily search cost below comes from my memory of its docs, not the pricing page, so please check it.\n\n**Tavily**\n- A basic search is 1 credit. The pricing page doesn't say this, so I'm relying on memory of the docs.\n- 15,000 searches is 15,000 credits.\n- Pay As You Go is $0.008 per credit, which comes to about **$120/month**.\n- The Project plan is $30 for 4,000 credits. If the other 11,000 credits are billed at the pay-as-you-go rate, that's about $118. The page doesn't state the overage rate.\n\n**Firecrawl**\n- Search costs 2 credits per 10 results, so 15,000 searches is about 30,000 credits.\n- The Standard plan has 100,000 credits for **$83/month** (billed yearly). That covers your volume with room to spare.\n- Hobby plus extra credits would cost more: $16–19 plus 25,000 extra credits at $5 per 1,000, so about $141–144.\n\n**Caveats**\n- If you request fewer than 10 results per search, Firecrawl may charge less than 2 credits. I can't confirm that from the page. At 1 credit per search, Hobby plus extras would be about $66.\n- Firecrawl's $83 is the yearly-billed price. Monthly billing costs more.\n- Firecrawl's search credits cover result excerpts. Full-page content for each result costs extra scrape credits, and Tavily's advanced search and extract calls also cost more than 1 credit. If you only need links and snippets, the comparison above holds.\n\nSources: [Tavily pricing](https://www.tavily.com/pricing), [Firecrawl pricing](https://www.firecrawl.dev/pricing)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":774,"cache_read_input_tokens":19009,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":774},"output_